WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 7.2 · Brand, Identity & Image
Brand strategy and promise

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Your brand promise is the experience you commit to deliver, from your very first activity or sale.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.763
Your brand promise is the experience you commit to deliver every time, from your very first activity or sale. A brand platform writes down that promise with the purpose, audiences, personality and messages behind it.

4
00:00:28.163 --> 00:00:28.763
The brand platform

5
00:00:28.763 --> 00:00:39.352
Purpose and promise: Why you exist and the experience people can count on. For example: A bakery training young people: “Real skills, in a real kitchen, from day one.”

6
00:00:39.352 --> 00:00:50.311
Audiences and personality: Who the brand speaks to and how it behaves, shaped by your values. For example: Trainees, local cafés as buyers and small funders; warm, practical and honest.

7
00:00:50.311 --> 00:01:00.159
Key messages: The few things you always say, adapted to each audience. For example: For cafés: fresh bread each morning, baked by trainees you could hire.

8
00:01:00.159 --> 00:01:10.096
Proof points: Evidence for the promise, or what you will measure and when. For example: First trainee results expected after the six-month pilot.

9
00:01:10.496 --> 00:01:11.096
Why it matters

10
00:01:11.096 --> 00:01:16.400
1. A promise people recognise sets you apart from the start.

11
00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:22.074
2. A kept promise builds trust when you have no track record.

12
00:01:22.074 --> 00:01:28.007
3. A broken promise damages trust faster than having none.

13
00:01:28.407 --> 00:01:29.007
What it guides

14
00:01:29.007 --> 00:01:33.941
1. Your voice, identity and guidelines, which express this platform.

15
00:01:33.941 --> 00:01:39.244
2. Your messaging framework, which takes its core message from it.

16
00:01:39.244 --> 00:01:45.548
3. Your MEAL data, which becomes your proof points over time.

17
00:01:45.948 --> 00:01:46.548
What to avoid

18
00:01:46.548 --> 00:01:51.852
Promising more than you can deliver at your current size.

19
00:01:51.852 --> 00:01:57.896
Saying the same words to every audience instead of keeping one promise.

20
00:01:57.896 --> 00:02:04.200
Inventing proof points: list the claims you will not make.

21
00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:06.600
You write the brand platform for what you are building.

22
00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:10.600
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:15.200
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
